### Document submission walkthrough (Visual Studio 2022 17.12+ / VS Code REST Client)
# Run `docker compose up` first. Execute the requests from top to bottom: later requests
# read the tokens and the submission Id from the named login and create responses.
# For JetBrains Rider or IntelliJ, use DocumentSubmission.Api.Rider.http instead.
# Seeded users: Alice (Editor, NL), Clara (Reviewer, NL). See README.md for all Ids.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080
@aliceEditor = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001
@claraReviewer = 10000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000003
@recordsOffice = 20000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001

### 0. Users that can log in (Development only)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/users

### 1. Log in as the editor
# @name editorLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{aliceEditor}}" }

### 2. Log in as the reviewer
# @name reviewerLogin
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "userId": "{{claraReviewer}}" }

### 3. Eligible reviewers and recipients in the editor's country
GET {{baseUrl}}/reviewers
Authorization: Bearer {{editorLogin.response.body.$.token}}

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/recipients
Authorization: Bearer {{editorLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 4. Create a submission (version 1) for Clara
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{editorLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WalkthroughBoundary

--WalkthroughBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="title"

Fictional annual report
--WalkthroughBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="reviewerId"

{{claraReviewer}}
--WalkthroughBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="comment"

First draft, ready for review.
--WalkthroughBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="draft.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../samples/draft.pdf
--WalkthroughBoundary--

### 5. The reviewer's work list
GET {{baseUrl}}/submissions
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 6. Reviewer returns version 1 with a comment
POST {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/return
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "versionNumber": 1, "comment": "Please add the summary table." }

### 7. Editor resubmits (version 2) with a comment on what changed
POST {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/resubmit
Authorization: Bearer {{editorLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=WalkthroughBoundary

--WalkthroughBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="comment"

Added the summary table.
--WalkthroughBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="file"; filename="revised.pdf"
Content-Type: application/pdf

< ../samples/revised.pdf
--WalkthroughBoundary--

### 8. Approving the old version 1 is rejected with 409 (stale versionNumber)
POST {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "versionNumber": 1 }

### 9. Reviewer approves version 2
POST {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/approve
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewerLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "versionNumber": 2 }

### 10. Editor distributes to a recipient
POST {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/distribute
Authorization: Bearer {{editorLogin.response.body.$.token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "recipientId": "{{recordsOffice}}" }

### 11. Details: all versions, approved version, recipient
GET {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}
Authorization: Bearer {{editorLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 12. Download version 1
GET {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/versions/1/content
Authorization: Bearer {{reviewerLogin.response.body.$.token}}

### 13. Audit trail
GET {{baseUrl}}/submissions/{{create.response.body.$.id}}/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{editorLogin.response.body.$.token}}
